content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent dose reduction table for AMG 510: text allows two dose reductions but table only shows two reductions (960→480→240), yet text says 'Dose reductions below 240 mg are not allowed' and 'Up to two dose reductions are allowed' – this is consistent, but the table in Table 6-2 shows only two dose levels after starting, which is correct. However, the text in Section 6.2.2.1 says 'Dose reductions below 240 mg are not allowed' but also says 'Subjects who experience an adverse event requiring dose reductions below 240 mg should be permanently discontinued' – this is contradictory because if below 240 is not allowed, then no one would require it. Actually, the issue is that the table shows Dose -2 as 240 mg, and the text says 'Dose reductions below 240 mg are not allowed' – this is fine, but the phrase 'requiring dose reductions below 240 mg' is impossible since it's not allowed. This is a minor inconsistency.",
      "page": 68,
      "quote": "Up to two dose reductions are allowed. Dose reductions below 240 mg are not allowed. Subjects who experience an adverse event requiring dose reductions below 240 mg should be permanently discontinued from AMG 510 treatment.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Docetaxel dose reduction table has 3 decrements but text allows only 2 dose reductions",
      "page": 71,
      "quote": "a If these toxicity events occur after the first dose reduction, then a second dose reduction is permitted. A third dose reduction is not permitted, and if toxicities continue after 2 dose decrements, then the subject should be discontinued from the study and enter the follow-up phase",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Docetaxel dose reduction table includes Dose -3 (discontinue) but text says only 2 dose reductions permitted",
      "page": 70,
      "quote": "Table 6-4. Dose Decrements for Docetaxel\nDocetaxel Doses (mg/m2)\nStarting Dose Dose -1 Dose -2 Dose -3\n75 55 37.5 Discontinue",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inclusion/exclusion criteria numbering skips from 208 to 209? Actually, the excerpt starts at 208? The text shows '208. Undetectable anti-HBs...' but the page starts with 'Undetectable anti-HBs' without a number, so the numbering is off. The first item on page 61 is not numbered, but it appears to be a continuation of a previous criterion. This is a formatting issue, not a factual error.",
      "page": 61,
      "quote": "Undetectable anti-HBs in this setting would suggest unclear and possible infection, and needs exclusion).",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Contradictory statements about rescreening: Section 5.4 says screen failures may be rescreened once (total ≤2), but then says 'Subjects who experience a technical failure of laboratory samples at screening... will not be considered a screen failure' – this is not contradictory, but the rescreening section says 'Refer to Section 8.1.1' which may not exist in the excerpt. Cross-reference to non-existent section.",
      "page": 63,
      "quote": "Individuals who do not meet the criteria for participation in this study (screen failure) due to reasons other than KRAS p.G12C mutation status may be rescreened once (total number of possible screenings ≤ 2). Refer to Section 8.1.1.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inclusion/exclusion criteria: Exclusion 214 says 'Therapeutic oral or intravenous antibiotics within 2 weeks prior to randomization' but Section 6.1.7 says 'Known strong inducers of CYP 3A4... within 14 days or 5 half-lives' – not contradictory, but the exclusion criteria list is missing a criterion for 'Prior/Concomitant Therapy' that includes 'Other investigational procedures are excluded' (219) which is vague.",
      "page": 61,
      "quote": "219. Other investigational procedures are excluded",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent contraception duration: Exclusion 226 says 'during treatment and for an additional 7 days after the last dose of AMG 510 or during treatment with docetaxel and 6 months after last dose of docetaxel' – but for AMG 510, the additional 7 days seems too short for a drug with a long half-life? Not necessarily an error, but the protocol should specify the half-life. However, the text says '7 days' for AMG 510 and '6 months' for docetaxel, which is plausible.",
      "page": 62,
      "quote": "Female subject is pregnant or breastfeeding or planning to become pregnant or breastfeed during treatment and for an additional 7 days after the last dose of AMG 510 or during treatment with docetaxel and 6 months after last dose of docetaxel if planning to become pregnant.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing information: The protocol does not specify the total sample size or randomization ratio in the excerpt, but that may be in another section. However, the excerpt includes 'Study 20190009' but no sample size. This is a missing critical element.",
      "page": 66,
      "quote": "There will be no non-investigational products in Study 20190009.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent use of 'randomization' vs 'enrollment': Section 5.3 says 'A subject is considered enrolled when the investigator decides that the subject has met all eligibility criteria' but then says 'Each subject who enters into the screening period... receives a unique subject identification number' – this is fine, but the protocol uses 'randomization' in exclusion criteria (e.g., 'within 3 years prior to randomization') and 'study day 1' elsewhere, which may be inconsistent if randomization is not the same as day 1.",
      "page": 61,
      "quote": "209. Malignancy other than NSCLC within 3 years prior to randomization",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Table 6-1, the AMG 510 dosage form description is garbled: '20 mg/1 mL single dose vial: 20 mg' appears under AMG 510, but AMG 510 is oral, not IV. The table seems to have mixed up the descriptions for AMG 510 and docetaxel. The text says 'Solid dosage form in strengths of 120 mg' but then '20 mg/1 mL single dose vial' – this is a clear error.",
      "page": 65,
      "quote": "20 mg/1 mL single dose vial: 20 mg\nSolid dosage form in strengths of 120 mg. The 120 mg coated tablet is presented as docetaxel in 1 mL in 50/50 (v/v) ratio",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Table 6-1, the docetaxel dosage form description is also garbled: '80 mg/4 mL single-dose vial: 80 mg' is correct, but the text says 'docetaxel in 4 mL 50/50 (v/v) ratio polysorbate 80/dehydrated alcohol' – this is fine, but the AMG 510 description includes 'polysorbate 80/dehydrated alcohol' which is for docetaxel, not AMG 510. This is a critical error in the table.",
      "page": 65,
      "quote": "film-coated yellow, oblong, debossed tablet. Excipients used in the tablets include lactose monohydrate, microcrystalline cellulose, croscarmellose sodium, magnesium stearate and Opadry® II Yellow. 80 mg/4 mL single-dose vial: 80 mg docetaxel in 4 mL 50/50 (v/v) ratio polysorbate 80/dehydrated alcohol",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "title": "In Table 6-1, the 'Dosage Formulation' row is missing for AMG 510, and the text is jumbled. The table header says 'Amgen Investigational Product' and 'Non-Amgen Investigational Product' but the rows are not properly separated. This is a formatting error that could lead to misinterpretation.",
      "page": 65,
      "quote": "Dosage Formulation\nlactose monohydrate, microcrystalline cellulose, croscarmellose sodium, magnesium 80 mg/4 mL single-dose vial: 80 mg",
      "severity": "major"
    }
  ]
}
